## 3. Token-Level Document Mutation & Canvas Diffing Mechanics

### 3.1 Surgical Patching vs. Full Rewrite Economics
In complex software engineering and long-form document writing, modifying an existing artifact must not require re-emitting the entire document.

Figure 04.03 compares the unit economics and latency of full document rewrites versus surgical canvas diffing.

![Figure 04.03: Token-Level Document Mutation & Canvas Diffing](../assets/svg/diag_ch04_document_canvas_diffing.svg)

As illustrated in Figure 04.03:
- **Full Rewrite Antipattern**: A 5,000-word document requiring a 10-line modification incurs a 5,000-token output tax ($0.075) and takes 45 seconds to generate.
- **Targeted Canvas Patching**: By instructing Claude to emit a surgical replacement chunk, the modification consumes only 35 output tokens ($0.0005) and executes in under 800 milliseconds!

